   "md": "# R2 · Not interested\n\n**Use case:** Polite close when a principal says no.\n\n**When it's sent:** When the principal replies \"no thanks\" or says no on a call. The lead moves to **Declined**.\n\n**Why:** Honors the opt-out promised in E1–E3, leaves the door open, and keeps the relationship clean.\n\n**Stage after logging as sent:** Declined\n\n## Notes\n\n- Also the follow-up for the call outcome \"Not interested\" in [[C1 · Call script - principal opened the email]].\n\n## Subject\n\n```text\nRe: Your {{school}} family message is ready\n```\n\n## Body\n\n```text\nHi {{greeting}},\n\nUnderstood, and thanks for the quick answer. I won't follow up again.\n\nIf things change, or a parent asks you about online safety down the road, just reply here and I'll pick it right back up.\n\nBest,\n{{sender}}\nCyberSafely.ai\n```\n\n## What changed and why\n\n- **Gives a reason to come back** (a parent asking), so the door stays open without any pressure.\n- Subject follows E1's new subject.\n\n## Refinement notes\n\n- \n\n## Previous version (from the app, Oct 8)\n\n<details><summary>Show</summary>\n\n```text\nSubject: Re: Free online-safety app for {{school}} families\n\nHi {{greeting}},\n\nThanks for letting me know. I won't follow up again. If anything changes, the offer stands. Just reply to this email.\n\nBest,\n{{sender}}\nCyberSafely.ai\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\nAfter refining, paste the subject and body back into the Outreach Manager (Templates tab). See [[Email Flow]].\n"
