   "md": "# N1 · Newsletter blurb (~50 words)\n\n**Use case:** About 50-word version of the family message for newsletters.\n\n**When it's sent:** Never sent on its own. It is inserted into G1, G2 and G3 as `{{newsletter}}`.\n\n**Why:** Schools often reach families through newsletters, not forwarded emails. A short, ready-to-paste blurb lowers the effort.\n\n**Stage after logging as sent:** no change\n\n## Notes\n\n- Used in [[G1 · No sign-ups yet (nudge)]], [[G2 · First sign-ups - thank-you + reminder]] and [[G3 · Monthly update]].\n\n## Subject\n\n_None (script or blurb)._\n\n## Body\n\n```text\nFree for {{school}} families: a year of CyberSafely.ai, through a collaboration with MSBA. The parent app alerts you early if your 5th–9th grader may be facing bullying, grooming or other serious trouble online, so you can step in before it escalates. Sign up in a few minutes: {{signup_link}}\n```\n\n## What changed and why\n\n- **Starts with \"Free for {{school}} families\".** In a newsletter, the first three words decide whether a parent keeps reading.\n- Uses the company's detection wording. ⚠️ Needs approval.\n\n## Refinement notes\n\n- \n\n## Previous version (from the app, Oct 8)\n\n<details><summary>Show</summary>\n\n```text\nFree online-safety app for {{school}} families: through a collaboration between CyberSafely.ai and MSBA, families of 5th–9th graders can use CyberSafely.ai free for one year. It alerts parents when a child may be facing something serious online, like cyberbullying. Sign up in a few minutes: {{signup_link}}\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\nAfter refining, paste the subject and body back into the Outreach Manager (Templates tab). See [[Email Flow]].\n"
